  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Unchanged from phase 1",
      "items": [
        "Same Fetcher, Writer, window rules and bronze paths; only the medium moved from disk to S3",
        "Raw is still read in place as external tables; nothing is loaded",
        "Staging and marts are the same dbt models, repointed at a DuckLake target"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "New in phase 2",
      "items": [
        "Every mart build commits through the DuckLake catalog on RDS, so concurrent dbt pods are safe",
        "A Postgres-wire serving layer (PgBouncer + pg_duckdb) sits between marts and every reader",
        "Auth, row-level security and audit come from Postgres roles at that layer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Go transforms in phase 2",
      "items": [
        "Go reads marts over Postgres wire with pgx, not from S3 directly, so the catalog stays the single view of truth",
        "Output is still Parquet to bronze/derived through the same Writer",
        "dbt declares derived as a source, exactly as in phase 1"
      ]
    }
  ]
